<http://data.silknow.org/object/ca5ffa0a-3479-32d0-838a-2f4bf49a3d32/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Two rectangular pieces, \"George III and the Prince of Wales Hunting at Windsor\". Copperplate print in red (now brown) on natural tabby-woven cotton. a) shows three mounted men (Prince of Wales at left), a pack of hounds, a man holding a dead fox and another sounding a horn. b) shows a stag hunt in Windsor Great Park, with George III, the Prince of Wales, and other riding; castle upper left; part of inscription on tree trunk at lower right. Cotton browned; stains, Selvedge with two blue cords on left edge of a)."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/ca5ffa0a-3479-32d0-838a-2f4bf49a3d32> .

